  "spans": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "nodeId": "n3",
      "text": "As of 2015, approximately 6300 Mt of plastic waste had been generated, around 9% of which had been recycled, 12% was incinerated, and 79% was accumulated in landfills or the natural environment.",
      "contextBefore": ", and additives, we present the first global analysis of all mass-produced plastics ever manufactured. We estimate that 8300 million metric tons (Mt) as of virgin plastics have been produced to date. ",
      "contextAfter": " If current production and waste management trends continue, roughly 12,000 Mt of plastic waste will be in landfills or in the natural environment by 2050. INTRODUCTION. A world without plastics, or s",
      "start": 1134,
      "end": 1328,
      "extractSha256": "3b8c46d1e721509ec48ca19c7e450b798683001acc488970f210b731b2094298",
      "windowSha256": "e98d84165ace9dc5af46ee27f50baae7cad2ca8d4cf23f8ececbb6d5a66f952b",
      "fetchedAt": "2026-11-18T03:00:48.703Z",
      "waybackUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20210831190627/https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.1700782",
      "tier": "exact"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "nodeId": "n4",
      "text": "Source Plastics Waste Materials Source: http://www.cleanup.org.au/rubbishreport06/sources_rubbish.html Challenges for Plastic Waste Management Globally Plastic wastage is growing at an annual rate of 9% globally.",
      "contextBefore": "per day. • According to the Central Pollution Control Board in India, 60 major India cities produce combined 25,940 tones of plastic waste every day. • 60% Of the Waste produced is recycled in India. ",
      "contextAfter": " By 2040, there will be 1.3 billion tones of plastic wastes present in the environment globally. Only 14% of the world's plastic waste is recycled. Plastic wastage is growing at an annual rate of 9%. ",
      "start": 1062,
      "end": 1274,
      "extractSha256": "55ba867b352854b13ab9010f21751a23acbf6ef79f58a4a5e8ce0fff87fcb220",
